---
import StandardPageLayout from "../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
---
<StandardPageLayout title="Accessibility" description="Painting for Beginners is designed for readable, keyboard-accessible use across phones, tablets, and desktop browsers." noindex={true}>
  <h2>Our approach</h2>
  <p>Accessibility is part of the site's design and editorial process. We use semantic headings and landmarks, keyboard-operable navigation, visible focus indicators, descriptive link text, meaningful image alternatives, responsive layouts, and reduced-motion support.</p>
  <h2>Known preview limitation</h2>
  <p>The public accessibility contact channel is awaiting owner confirmation. That channel must be supplied and tested before final production signoff.</p>
  <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
  <p>When the contact channel is active, include the page address, a description of the barrier, and—if comfortable sharing—the browser, device, and assistive technology used. We will prioritize a practical route to the same information while investigating the underlying issue.</p>
</StandardPageLayout>
